db/ref 1083 #uuid "faf2a892-5d88-5731-80fa-930f46707b27" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559149 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559286 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559437 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559528 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559647 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "0ff2e77b-8d7a-52d3-9995-01bf83f68824" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559148 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559211 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559294 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559515 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186559634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186559634 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559674 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "38f6bcff-7304-5d0b-a0af-efe2d713e856" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559674 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1069 "q-139496" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. Any $5\\times 3$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nII. Any $3\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. The singular values of the matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ are negative." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "c14fd620-27ea-593f-816e-9c2134638c65" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559855 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. Since $A$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $3\\times 3$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{3\\times 5}\\times {A}_{5\\times 3}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{3\\times 3}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $3$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement II is false. Since $A$ is a $3\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 3$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 3}\\times {A}_{3\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. All singular values of any matrix are non-negative.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186559647 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1069 "q-95279" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1071 "Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The matrix $A=[\\begin{aligned}-2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]$ has two negative singular values.\n\nII. Any $4\\times 5$ matrix $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\nIII. Any $8\\times 4$ matrix $A$ has at most $8$ distinct singular values." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ffe00adb-b1a9-53a2-98b2-87735ab0e412" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559891 #edb/ref 1074 "The singular values of the matrix $A$ are the square roots of the eigenvalues of the matrix ${A}^{T}\\,A.$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our statements.\n\n- Statement I is false.  All singular values of any matrix are non-negative. So, \n$A$  can't have any negative singular value.\n\n- Statement II is true. Indeed, since $A$ is a $4\\times 5$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $5\\times 4$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $5\\times 5$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{5\\times 4}\\times {A}_{4\\times 5}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{5\\times 5}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $5$ distinct singular values.\n\n- Statement III is false. Since $A$ is a $8\\times 4$ matrix and ${A}^{T}$ is a $4\\times 8$ matrix, ${A}^{T}\\,A$ must be a $4\\times 4$ matrix: \n\n$$\n{{A}^{T}}_{4\\times 8}\\times {A}_{8\\times 4}={{A}^{T}\\,A}_{4\\times 4}\n$$\n\nHence, $A$ has at most $4$ distinct singular values.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559952 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186559969 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559952 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "92011cee-25ec-5645-8649-3c5082cdb2df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559952 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186404794 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559962 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186559973 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559962 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "b2c6bcad-aab2-51b4-8844-1a9ba59e06d8" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559962 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186543482 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559969 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186559972 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559969 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "c7261c21-321e-5abd-8187-70f19af061de" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559969 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186415578 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559972 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d141f860-642e-5d1b-b75f-8196aeaa74cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559972 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186559855 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559973 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186559952 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559973 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "d45aa491-e815-5760-826e-8fe2c46d302f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186559973 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186559891 #edb/ref 